DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ddeevvccttll library adjusts the state of devices in the kernel's internal
     device hierarchy.  Each control operation accepts a _d_e_v_i_c_e argument that
     identifies the device to adjust.  The _d_e_v_i_c_e may be specified as either
     the name of an existing device or as a bus-specific address.  The follow‐
     ing bus-specific address formats are currently supported:

           ppccii_d_o_m_a_i_n:_b_u_s:_s_l_o_t:_f_u_n_c_t_i_o_n
                   A PCI device with the specified _d_o_m_a_i_n, _b_u_s, _s_l_o_t, and
                   _f_u_n_c_t_i_o_n.

           ppccii_b_u_s:_s_l_o_t:_f_u_n_c_t_i_o_n
                   A PCI device in domain zero with the specified _b_u_s, _s_l_o_t,
                   and _f_u_n_c_t_i_o_n.

           _h_a_n_d_l_e  A device with an ACPI handle of _h_a_n_d_l_e.  The handle must be
                   specified as an absolute path and must begin with a “\”.

     The ddeevvccttll__aattttaacchh() function probes a device and attaches a suitable de‐
     vice driver if one is found.

     The ddeevvccttll__ddeettaacchh() function detaches a device from its current device
     driver.  The device is left detached until either a new driver for its
     parent bus is loaded or the device is explicitly probed via
     ddeevvccttll__aattttaacchh().  If _f_o_r_c_e is true, the current device driver will be de‐
     tached even if the device is busy.

     The ddeevvccttll__ddeelleettee() function deletes a device from the device tree.  No
     If _f_o_r_c_e is true, the device is deleted even if the device is physically
     present.

     The ddeevvccttll__ddiissaabbllee() function disables a device.  If the device is cur‐
     rently attached to a device driver, the device driver will be detached
     from the device, but the device will retain its current name.  If
     _f_o_r_c_e___d_e_t_a_c_h is true, the current device driver will be detached even if
     the device is busy.  The device will remain disabled and detached until
     it is explicitly enabled via ddeevvccttll__eennaabbllee().

     The ddeevvccttll__eennaabbllee() function re-enables a disabled device.  The device
     will probe and attach if a suitable device driver is found.

     The ddeevvccttll__ssuussppeenndd() function suspends a device.  This may include plac‐
     ing the device in a reduced power state, but any device driver currently
     attached to the device will remain attached.

     The ddeevvccttll__rreessuummee() function resumes a suspended device to a fully work‐
     ing state.

     The ddeevvccttll__sseett__ddrriivveerr() function attaches a device driver named _d_r_i_v_e_r to
     a device.  If the device is already attached and _f_o_r_c_e is false, the re‐
     quest will fail.  If the device is already attached and _f_o_r_c_e is true,
     the device will be detached from its current device driver before it is
     attached to the new device driver.

     The ddeevvccttll__cclleeaarr__ddrriivveerr() function resets a device so that it can be at‐
     tached to any valid device driver rather than only drivers with a previ‐
     ously specified name.  This function is used to undo a previous call to
     ddeevvccttll__sseett__ddrriivveerr().  If the device is already attached and _f_o_r_c_e is
     false, the request will fail.  If the device is already attached and
     _f_o_r_c_e is true, the device will be detached from its current device
     driver.  After the device's name is reset, it is reprobed and attached to
     a suitable device driver if one is found.

     The ddeevvccttll__rreessccaann() function rescans a bus device checking for devices
     that have been added or removed.

     The ddeevvccttll__ggeettppaatthh() retrieves the path to the _d_e_v_i_c_e from the kernel us‐
     ing the _l_o_c_a_t_o_r method to construct the path.  The _b_u_f_f_e_r pointer is up‐
     dated with an allocated buffer that must be freed with free(3).

     The ddeevvccttll__ffrreeeezzee() function freezes probe and attach processing initi‐
     ated in response to drivers being loaded.

     The ddeevvccttll__tthhaaww() function resumes (thaws the freeze) probe and attach
     processing initiated in response to drivers being loaded.

     The ddeevvccttll__rreesseett() function resets the specified device using bus-spe‐
     cific reset method.  The _d_e_t_a_c_h argument, if true, specifies that the de‐
     vice driver is detached before the reset, and re-attached afterwards.  If
     false, the device is suspended before the reset, and resumed after.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     The ddeevvccttll__aattttaacchh(), ddeevvccttll__cclleeaarr__ddrriivveerr(), ddeevvccttll__ddeelleettee(),
     ddeevvccttll__ddeettaacchh(), ddeevvccttll__ddiissaabbllee(), ddeevvccttll__eennaabbllee(), ddeevvccttll__ssuussppeenndd(),
     ddeevvccttll__rreessccaann(), ddeevvccttll__rreessuummee(), and ddeevvccttll__aattttaacchh00() functions return
     the value 0 if successful; otherwise the value -1 is returned and the
     global variable _e_r_r_n_o is set to indicate the error.

EERRRROORRSS
     In addition to specific errors noted below, all of the ddeevvccttll functions
     may fail for any of the errors described in open(2) as well as:

     [EINVAL]           The device name is too long.

     [ENOENT]           No existing device matches the specified name or loca‐
                        tion.

     [EPERM]            The current process is not permitted to adjust the
                        state of _d_e_v_i_c_e.

     The ddeevvccttll__aattttaacchh() function may fail if:

     [EBUSY]            The device is already attached.

     [ENOMEM]           An internal memory allocation request failed.

     [ENXIO]            The device is disabled.

     [ENXIO]            No suitable driver for the device could be found, or
                        the driver failed to attach.

     The ddeevvccttll__ddeettaacchh() function may fail if:

     [EBUSY]            The current device driver for _d_e_v_i_c_e is busy and can‐
                        not detach at this time.  Note that some drivers may
                        return this even if _f_o_r_c_e is true.

     [ENXIO]            The device is not attached to a driver.

     [ENXIO]            The current device driver for _d_e_v_i_c_e does not support
                        detaching.

     The ddeevvccttll__eennaabbllee() function may fail if:

     [EBUSY]            The device is already enabled.

     [ENOMEM]           An internal memory allocation request failed.

     [ENXIO]            No suitable driver for the device could be found, or
                        the driver failed to attach.

     The ddeevvccttll__ddiissaabbllee() function may fail if:

     [EBUSY]            The current device driver for _d_e_v_i_c_e is busy and can‐
                        not detach at this time.  Note that some drivers may
                        return this even if _f_o_r_c_e___d_e_t_a_c_h is true.

     [ENXIO]            The device is already disabled.

     [ENXIO]            The current device driver for _d_e_v_i_c_e does not support
                        detaching.

     The ddeevvccttll__ssuussppeenndd() function may fail if:

     [EBUSY]            The device is already suspended.

     [EINVAL]           The device to be suspended is the root bus device.

     The ddeevvccttll__rreessuummee() function may fail if:

     [EINVAL]           The device is not suspended.

     [EINVAL]           The device to be resumed is the root bus device.

     The ddeevvccttll__sseett__ddrriivveerr() function may fail if:

     [EBUSY]            The device is currently attached to a device driver
                        and _f_o_r_c_e is false.

     [EBUSY]            The current device driver for _d_e_v_i_c_e is busy and can‐
                        not detach at this time.

     [EFAULT]           The _d_r_i_v_e_r argument points outside the process' allo‐
                        cated address space.

     [ENOENT]           No device driver with the requested name exists.

     [ENOMEM]           An internal memory allocation request failed.

     [ENXIO]            The device is disabled.

     [ENXIO]            The new device driver failed to attach.

     The ddeevvccttll__cclleeaarr__ddrriivveerr() function may fail if:

     [EBUSY]            The device is currently attached to a device driver
                        and _f_o_r_c_e is false.

     [EBUSY]            The current device driver for _d_e_v_i_c_e is busy and can‐
                        not detach at this time.

     [EINVAL]           The device is not configured for a specific device
                        driver name.

     [ENXIO]            The device driver chosen after reprobing failed to at‐
                        tach.

     The ddeevvccttll__rreessccaann() function may fail if:

     [ENXIO]            The device is not attached to a driver.

     [ENXIO]            The bus driver does not support rescanning.

     The ddeevvccttll__ddeelleettee() function may fail if:

     [EBUSY]            The device is physically present and _f_o_r_c_e is false.

     [EINVAL]           _d_e_v is the root device of the device tree.

     The ddeevvccttll__rreesseett() function may fail if:

     [ENXIO]            The bus does not implement the reset method.

     [ETIMEDOUT]        The device failed to respond after the reset in the
                        time limits specific to the bus.
     The ddeevvccttll__rreesseett() function may also return errors caused by the attach,
     detach, suspend, and resume methods of the device driver.

