HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The ddeevvccttll library first appeared in FreeBSD 10.3.

BBUUGGSS
     If a device is suspended individually via ddeevvccttll__ssuussppeenndd() and the entire
     machine is subsequently suspended, the device will be resumed when the
     machine resumes.

     Similarly, if the device is suspended, and ddeevvccttll__rreesseett() is called on
     the device with _d_e_t_a_c_h set to _f_a_l_s_e, the device is resumed by the
     ddeevvccttll__rreesseett() call.  Or, if the driver for the device is detached manu‐
     ally, and ddeevvccttll__rreesseett() is called on the device with _d_e_t_a_c_h set to _t_r_u_e,
     device reset re-attaches the driver.

